# stow ignore list for the zsh package.
#
# NOTE: this file REPLACES stow's built-in defaults, so the standard entries are
# repeated below — dropping them would start stowing .git metadata and editor
# backups into $HOME.
#
# perf-baseline.md is documentation and .zcompdump* are zsh completion-cache
# artifacts (already gitignored) that zsh writes into the repo dir. Neither
# belongs in $HOME.
^/perf-baseline\.md
^/\.zcompdump.*

# --- stow defaults, preserved ---
RCS
.+,v
CVS
\.\#.+
\.cvsignore
\.svn
_darcs
\.hg
\.git
\.gitignore
\.gitmodules
.+~
\#.*\#
^/README.*
^/LICENSE.*
^/COPYING
